1
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,740
Mr. Ling, we'd like to toast you.

2
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,400
Keep up the good work.

3
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,430
It's too noisy here. I'll head back first.

4
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,080
What will I do if you leave?

5
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:32,439
I'll come back if you're in danger.

6
00:00:32,439 --> 00:00:33,240
No.

7
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,400
I have a task for you later.

8
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:37,800
A task?

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,640
Mr. Ling.

10
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:42,860
Xiaoya did a good job this time.

11
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:44,260
Keep working hard in the future.

12
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,500
Quick, offer Mr. Ling another toast.

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,430
Thank you, Mr. Ling. A toast to you.

14
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:50,600
Keep an eye on Muchen.

15
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,700
If those people try to harm her again later,

16
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,360
remember to gather evidence.

17
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,600
You really treat me like a subordinate.

18
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:00,870
So, are you going or not?

19
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:03,940
Mr. Ling.

20
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,039
I really like the new live-streaming model.

21
00:01:10,039 --> 00:01:12,600
The girls you paired up are all excellent.

22
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:13,720
In the future,

23
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:16,380
I will lead them to achieve even better results.

24
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,400
Here's to you.

25
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,300
Mr. Ling.

26
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:38,000
Why don't you come over and drink with us?

27
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,600
After all, it's a celebration for the streamers.

28
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:42,740
I didn't do much.

29
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:46,340
If it weren't for you,

30
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:49,830
Muchen would probably have left the company.

31
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:51,660
If you put it that way,

32
00:01:51,759 --> 00:01:53,490
it seems I did contribute a lot.

33
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,120
Do you really not like those rewards?

34
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,800
I just feel

35
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:08,639
like I haven't made any real contribution,

36
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:11,990
and I don't deserve the rewards from the management.

37
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:13,660
Why would you think that?

38
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:18,860
Maybe I just lack a sense of security.

39
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:21,720
Mr. Ling,

40
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,820
Mr. Wang is calling Muchen over.

41
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,200
Why so distant after just a few days?

42
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,980
Of course not, Mr. Wang.

43
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,380
Mr. Wang.

44
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,400
Thank you for giving me so many votes today.

45
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,980
If it weren't for you,

46
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:14,780
I definitely wouldn't have won.

47
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,040
Here's a toast to you.

48
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,600
No need to be so polite.

49
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,880
With me here, you won't lose.

50
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,200
Come, pour another glass.

51
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:40,180
Come on, Chengcheng,

52
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,740
have a drink.

53
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:42,580
Come on.

54
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:44,380
Mr. Wang, I can't drink anymore.

55
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,200
Have a drink.

56
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,680
Hurry up.

57
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:49,480
Have a drink.

58
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,000
Let me tell you,

59
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,860
let's drink with crossed arms.

60
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,280
Come on.

61
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:04,620
It's fine.

62
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:07,540
Come on, pour another one.

63
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:10,650
Chengcheng.

64
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:12,640
Mr. Wang,

65
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,640
I have work tomorrow.

66
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:15,810
Chengcheng.

67
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:17,950
Chengcheng, you...

68
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:20,140
Get away.

69
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,460
It's not like I haven't slept with you before.

70
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:25,860
Stop playing hard to get.

71
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:28,780
Let me go. Let go.

72
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,510
Bro, what do you think she tastes like?

73
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:34,870
How would I know if I haven't tried?

74
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:37,250
When we get rich, we'll get one too.

75
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,240
Let go.

76
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Let me go.

77
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,680
Who let you in?

78
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,300
What are you doing?

79
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:49,780
Don't mind me. Continue.

80
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:09,380
Where is the boss?

81
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:10,340
I don't know.

82
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:12,140
Go check outside.

83
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:12,840
Let's go.

84
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:16,360
I don't know

85
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:20,180
what kind of trash this guy is.

86
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:37,200
Mr. Ling, we still can't reach Mucheng.

87
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,460
Don't worry about him.

88
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:41,280
Let's go.

89
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:42,800
I'll take you home.

90
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:44,380
No need.

91
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,940
When a girl is drunk,

92
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,140
she shouldn't just get into a man's car.

93
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:52,840
Especially a handsome one.

94
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,440
Don't worry about me.

95
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:57,800
You guys go ahead.

96
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,900
Attorney Gu, go home and rest early then.

97
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:03,040
Don't worry. Bye.

98
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,640
Help me.

99
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:36,340
Let me go.

100
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,980
Where are you taking me?

101
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:12,620
Where are you taking me?

102
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:13,000
Home.

103
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:17,740
Did you finish the task I gave you?

104
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:19,180
Wait a minute.

105
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:22,140
Look.

106
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,740
What is this?

107
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:29,800
It's so blurry. What can you even see?

108
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:32,140
It wasn't me. I was late,

109
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:33,340
so I only took one picture.

110
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:34,600
What happened?

111
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:36,200
How could you be late?

112
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:38,380
That's because I...

113
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,640
It's because...

114
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:45,370
That guy had several bodyguards protecting him.

115
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:46,940
In that situation,

116
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:49,040
I had to use my powers to escape.

117
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:49,540
You know?

118
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:51,140
It was extremely dangerous.

119
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,980
Were you hurt?

120
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:55,440
They alone couldn't hurt me.

121
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,640
But I didn't get the evidence for you.

122
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,640
It's a real pity.

123
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,940
You can't be so reckless in the future.

124
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:03,940
Okay.

125
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,480
It was so dangerous.

126
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:09,600
What if something happened to you?

127
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:11,080
Got it.

128
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,880
If you can't hold your liquor, you shouldn't drink anymore.

129
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,680
How is my alcohol tolerance bad?

130
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:18,480
I'm a good drinker.

131
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:20,440
Look, I've been drinking all night,

132
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,100
and I'm still perfectly fine.

133
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,080
So many stars.

134
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:34,800
Look, there are so many stars.

135
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,640
Didn't you say you were some kind of soul...

136
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,140
soul ferryman?

137
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,580
Can you be like those superheroes in comics,

138
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,600
and just fly away with a whoosh?

139
00:09:50,540 --> 00:09:51,540
I can't fly.

140
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:54,800
You can't even fly.

141
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,940
You're not impressive at all.

142
00:09:58,780 --> 00:09:59,960
What are you doing?

143
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,080
What are comics?

144
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,240
Are the people in them very powerful?

145
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:05,360
Very powerful.

146
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:07,000
Everyone in them can fly.

147
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
They are all more powerful than you.

148
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:19,520
Are you trying to murder me?

149
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,680
Didn't you ask me to bring you here?

150
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:23,640
Take me back quickly. I'm scared.

151
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,640
Look.

152
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,780
It's so beautiful.

153
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:37,780
It's been a long time since someone

154
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,780
watched the stars with me like this.

155
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,970
Let me test you with a question.

156
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:48,780
Test me?

157
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,060
You definitely won't be able to answer it.

158
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:52,140
What a joke.

159
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:55,460
Are the stars in the sky?

160
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,280
Are airplanes also in the sky?

161
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:00,580
Yes.

162
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:03,260
Then when airplanes fly in the sky,

163
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,640
why don't they hit the stars?

164
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,540
You're testing me with such common sense?

165
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:07,800
Then tell me.

166
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,580
That's because

167
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,640
stars exist in the galaxy beyond the sky,

168
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:15,180
so airplanes naturally can't reach them.

169
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:15,980
Wrong.

170
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:19,040
It's because stars can dodge.

171
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:23,360
I told you you couldn't guess it.

172
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,080
You...

173
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,880
You're talking nonsense.

174
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:28,840
When I was little,

175
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,980
my dad told me this joke.

176
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,040
The stars are really beautiful.

177
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,440
Xingcan, are the stars pretty?

178
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:41,940
Pretty.

179
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:46,280
Xingcan is also a star in Dad's heart.

180
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,600
So in the future, Xingcan

181
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:51,200
must also be like the stars in the night sky,

182
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:52,740
bright and dazzling.

183
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:53,940
Okay.
